# The build reads the Dockerfile and the files it copies. Everything
# else here is documentation, checks, and configuration, and Docker
# leaves it out of the build context. The recipe hash covers the build
# context, so a change to one of these files needs no new revision,
# except package.toml: the recipe hashes it on its own.
README.md
AGENTS.md
LICENSE
package.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
smoke/
# The shim's tests and the target that runs them are checks, not
# inputs of the binary.
shim/*_test.go
shim/Makefile
